---
import FrameworkLayout from '../../layouts/FrameworkLayout.astro';

const sections = ['Overview', 'The Four Perspectives', 'Defining Metrics', 'Alignment Across Organization', 'Implementation Tips'];
---

<FrameworkLayout title="Balanced Scorecard" sections={sections}>
  <h1 id="overview">Balanced Scorecard</h1>
  
  <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
  <p>
    The Balanced Scorecard translates an organization's vision and strategy into a comprehensive set of performance measures. Developed by Robert Kaplan and David Norton, it moves beyond financial metrics to provide a balanced view of organizational performance.
  </p>
  <p>
    This framework ensures that strategic objectives are cascaded throughout the organization and aligned with measurable outcomes.
  </p>

  <h2 id="the-four-perspectives">The Four Perspectives</h2>
  
  <h3>1. Financial Perspective</h3>
  <p>
    Traditional financial metrics: revenue growth, profitability, return on investment, cash flow. These measure the tangible outcomes of strategy execution.
  </p>

  <h3>2. Customer Perspective</h3>
  <p>
    How do customers perceive your value? Metrics include customer satisfaction, retention, market share, and customer lifetime value.
  </p>

  <h3>3. Internal Process Perspective</h3>
  <p>
    What internal processes must excel to deliver customer value? Measure innovation, operational efficiency, quality, and cycle time.
  </p>

  <h3>4. Learning & Growth Perspective</h3>
  <p>
    What capabilities and culture do you need to sustain success? Track employee satisfaction, retention, skill development, and innovation capacity.
  </p>

  <h2 id="defining-metrics">Defining Metrics</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Articulate strategic objectives for each perspective</li>
    <li>Select 3-5 key performance indicators (KPIs) per perspective</li>
    <li>Set targets and measurement intervals</li>
    <li>Link cause-and-effect relationships across perspectives</li>
    <li>Create strategic initiatives to close performance gaps</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="alignment-across-organization">Alignment Across Organization</h2>
  <p>
    Cascade the Balanced Scorecard throughout the organization. Each department and team develops their own scorecards that support corporate strategy. This creates alignment and ensures everyone understands how their work contributes to strategic success.
  </p>

  <h2 id="implementation-tips">Implementation Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Start with clear strategic clarity at the top</li>
    <li>Involve frontline teams in metric selection</li>
    <li>Focus on leading indicators, not just lagging indicators</li>
    <li>Review regularly and adjust as strategy evolves</li>
    <li>Link performance management and compensation to scorecard</li>
    <li>Use visual dashboards for real-time monitoring</li>
  </ul>
</FrameworkLayout>
